{
  "_comment": "Canonical content set. Every conformance target projects this into its own CMS; every contract assertion refers to it rather than to per-CMS literals. `type` values are canonical names \u2014 each target maps them to its CMS's real type via Target.types. No template documents here: the frontend forces a layout only on paths it is not excluded from, and the journey's roots are excluded, so nothing needs them. They were seeded when forcing was still on for /news, and every WordPress test re-seeds \u2014 the extra document pushed two tests past the 30s timeout. Re-seed them if forcing is ever enabled for a journey root; templates ARE CMS content and each target must carry the ones its frontend references. THREE LEVELS DEEP on purpose: /news/first-post/update is a grandchild of /news. Without one, a listing scoped to a path cannot be told apart from one scoped to direct children \u2014 the subtree test passed whichever an adapter returned, which is how the two came to disagree.",
